Bug fix: every page that started at about:blank left a web process behind.

WebKit keeps one spare, "prewarmed" web process ready for the next page.
When a page needs a process and has no site yet (a new view loading
about:blank or a string, which is how every tab a CDP client opens starts),
WebProcessPool::tryTakePrewarmedProcess() picks the spare, removes it from
the pool's set of spares, and only then checks whether the sandbox is on, in
which case it returns nothing and the page gets a new process instead. The
sandbox setting is on by default in this API whether or not Bubblewrap is
compiled in. The spare was then in no set and attached to no page, so
nothing ever shut it down, and the pool started another spare to replace it.
One process of 100 MiB and more leaked for each such page; 300 pages opened
and closed over CDP left 300 processes.

Make the check before the spare is removed. It is also only meaningful when
the processes really run under Bubblewrap, where a spare is tied to the
primary data store; in a build without Bubblewrap the spare is now used, as
on other platforms, so new pages also start faster.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebProcessPool.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebProcessPool.cpp
@@ -882,16 +882,18 @@
 
     WTFEmitSignpost(this, ProcessPrewarming, "Using prewarmed process with pid %d", prewarmedProcess->processID());
 
-    bool didRemove = m_prewarmedProcesses.remove(*prewarmedProcess);
-    ASSERT_UNUSED(didRemove, didRemove);
-
-#if PLATFORM(GTK) || PLATFORM(WPE)
+#if (PLATFORM(GTK) || PLATFORM(WPE)) && ENABLE(BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX)
     // In platforms using Bubblewrap for sandboxing, prewarmed process is launched using the WebProcessPool primary WebsiteDataStore,
     // so we don't use it in case of using a different WebsiteDataStore.
+    // zebkit: decided before the process is taken out of the pool's set, not after, which left it
+    // running with nothing that would ever shut it down.
     if (m_sandboxEnabled)
         return nullptr;
 #endif
 
+    bool didRemove = m_prewarmedProcesses.remove(*prewarmedProcess);
+    ASSERT_UNUSED(didRemove, didRemove);
+
     ASSERT(prewarmedProcess->isPrewarmed());
     prewarmedProcess->setWebsiteDataStore(websiteDataStore);
     prewarmedProcess->markIsNoLongerInPrewarmedPool();
